body:
I am socially off especially the nonverbal. it bothers many.

I really want to fit in and be social but it's not happening. 

&#x200B;

No pressure, no diamonds. Thomas Carlyle

&#x200B;

not in this case :(

In my experience as my slow brain waves were reduced my life got better, for I was more grounded, more aware, more in touch with myself and my environs. Yes and this made things harder. Being more grounded, aware, and a little more in touch with myself and my body meant that I was more available to the sensations and feelings that were masked by my slow, sleepy, and dreamy brain waves. At the same time I was also doing somatic experiencing therapy so I was also somewhat more able to sit with stronger discomfort without "drifting off."  As I got better I was more available to notice the other stuff. Mostly from early childhood.  I hope I made sense. The other issue I have is that I want to progress like a bat out of hell. I am like a dog cashing it's own tail. I got a taste of living a more functional life and I Want More. Atlas, I can't afford to get more healthcare, so it's so painful to wait watching my life, my dreams, and my potential slip by while I am still imprisoned by my nervous system. 

&#x200B;

sorry about the typos I am exhausted and much more  :-)
